@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Clinical trial detail page: one trial, laid out in its section anchors\nA click opens it, the trial record is an external registry's, and the page reconciles on its one required member

actor "Person / Client" as P
participant "Gate\n(transport facade)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices)" as UN
database "sessions + render ledger\n(repo rows)" as REPO
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(FindCare)" as PXY
participant "clinical_trial_detail tool\n(FindCare)" as CTD
participant "Prose tool\n(SharedServices)" as PROSE
participant "ClinicalTrials.gov\n(external registry)" as CTG

P -> GATE : click a trial's link (gesture)\naction 'clinical_trial_detail', params {nctId}\nAccept: application/x-ndjson
note right of GATE
  The gate is dumb transport: it collects the session
  token, the HTTP head and the params, streams the
  answer back, verifies nothing and owns no route.
end note
GATE -> UN : pass(session_token, head, params)

== Triage: which of the five call types ==
UN -> UN : the arrival carries a session token\n-> client_sessioned route (proof: session_token)
UN -> REPO : load session by GUID
UN -> UN : verify token + restamp nonce\n(session-security helpers)
note right of UN
  Triage is by declared proof. A session token means a
  client we served index.html -- not tool_to_tool (none),
  not third_party_callback (api_key), not static_witness
  (none), not internal_callback (our_signature).
end note

== Determine page + record the render ledger ==
UN -> UN : read the map: this request builds the\nclinical_trial_detail page (subject: clinical_trial)
UN -> REPO : ledger: record required_members = [clinical_trial_detail];\nmembers also include prose
note left of REPO
  Dispatch records the page's required_members as
  expectations; each completion callback (our_signature)
  closes one; the completeness budget races them. This
  is a gesture, so no UtteranceManager mining runs --
  the click already names the trial.
end note

== Dispatch: the required member, then prose on its facts ==
UN -> PXY : dispatch clinical_trial_detail (tool_to_tool)
PXY -> CTD : relay locally (function call)
CTD -> CTG : query the trial by NCT id\n(external registry, not ours)
CTG --> CTD : trial record, or nothing
CTD -> CTD : lay the trial into its section anchors\n(recursion-guarded)
CTD --> PXY : trial detail document
PXY --> UN : internal_callback (proof: our_signature)
UN -> REPO : ledger: close clinical_trial_detail (required);\nmerge serially -- a conflict RAISES

UN -> PROSE : dispatch prose with the trial facts\n(member, not required)
PROSE -> PROSE : compose the user-facing sentence\n(one model call, pydantic-ai)
PROSE --> UN : answers directly (co-resident with the main)
UN -> REPO : ledger: close prose; merge serially

== Reconcile + respond ==
alt required member closed within the completeness budget
  UN -> UN : page reconciled\n(required_members all closed)
  UN -> GATE : stream the page events\n(the gate owns the one stream)
  GATE --> P : the trial in its sections, with prose
else the required member times out, dies, or a merge conflicts
  UN -> REPO : ledger raises: on_missing_required / on_conflict;\nor the render_timeout_seconds budget expires
  UN -> GATE : stream the layman on_timeout explanation
  GATE --> P : plain-English "we could not load this trial in time"
end

note over UN, REPO #f3f4f6
  Page error management, all instrumented with timings at a severity
  matching impact:
  - timeout -> the navigator responds anyway with the layman on_timeout text
  - conflict -> merging the returning documents raises (on_conflict = raise)
  - missing required -> a dead or never-returning clinical_trial_detail raises
    (on_missing_required = raise). prose is not required, so its absence
    does not block the page.
  Every throw ends here in the UniversalNavigator; the FindCare proxy
  re-raises, never swallows.
end note

@enduml
